I. NON-FUNCTIONAL REQUIREMENTS
1. Product Requirements
1.1. Usability Requirements
- Users shall be able to learn how to use the Course Registration System within 30 minutes.
- Students should be able to complete common tasks, such as logging in, searching for courses, registering for courses, and canceling registrations, in no more than 3–4 steps.
- The user interface shall have a consistent layout, buttons, colors, menus, and notification messages across all screens.
- The system shall display clear and understandable error messages when users enter invalid information or perform unsuccessful operations.
- The system shall support Vietnamese to make it easier for students to use.
1.2. Efficiency Requirements
a) Performance Requirements:
- The application shall start within 3–5 seconds on an ordinary computer.
- User login shall be processed within 2 seconds under normal operating conditions.
- Searching for courses and displaying the course list shall take no more than 3 seconds.
- Registering or canceling a course shall be processed within 2 seconds under normal operating conditions.
- The system shall support multiple students accessing the course registration system simultaneously.
b) Space Requirements:
- The application shall use no more than 200 MB of memory under normal operating conditions, excluding database storage.
- The application shall run without requiring special hardware or a dedicated graphics card.
- The database shall store student information, course information, and registration records efficiently.
- The system shall regularly back up registration data to prevent data loss in case of unexpected failures.
1.3. Dependability Requirements
- The system shall achieve a target successful operation rate of at least 90% under normal operating conditions.
- The system shall be available during the university's course registration periods.
- Unexpected system failures shall not result in incomplete or duplicate course registration records.
- The system shall validate registration information before saving it to the database.
- The system shall display an error message within 3 seconds when a registration operation fails.
- The system shall maintain data consistency when multiple students register for the same course simultaneously.
1.4. Security Requirements
- Users shall log in using their student ID and password.
- Passwords shall be hashed using a secure algorithm such as bcrypt and shall never be stored in plain text.
- The system shall prevent unauthorized users from accessing student registration information.
- Every database query shall use parameterized statements to prevent SQL injection attacks.
- Students shall only be allowed to view and modify their own course registration information.
- The system shall validate user input to prevent invalid or malicious data.
- Users shall be logged out securely when they choose the logout function.
2. Organizational Requirements
2.1. Environmental Requirements
- The application shall run on Windows 10 and Windows 11 operating systems.
- The minimum hardware requirements shall include:
  - CPU: 2-core processor.
  - RAM: 4 GB.
  - Free disk space: 2 GB.
- The system shall support modern web browsers such as Google Chrome, Microsoft Edge, and Firefox.
- The system shall require an Internet connection when accessing the online registration system.
2.2. Operational Requirements
- Each student shall have a unique student ID and password to verify their identity.
- Students shall log in before accessing course registration functions.
- The system shall automatically update available course seats after successful registration or cancellation.
- The system shall provide clear notifications for successful and unsuccessful registration operations.
- Database backup and recovery procedures shall be performed regularly.
- Administrators shall monitor course registration information and system operation.
2.3. Development Requirements
- Programming language: Python.
- Database management system: SQLite (for the current prototype); PostgreSQL may be used for future deployment.
- Documentation, source code, and team management: GitHub.
- Drawing DFD, Use Case, Class Diagram, and Database Schema
- GUI design: Figma.
- Creating test cases: Microsoft Excel.
- Programming IDE: Visual Studio Code.
- Bug tracking tools: Bugzilla.
- Unit testing: pytest (Python).
- Packaging and deployment: Docker (if required for deployment).
3. External Requirements
3.1. Legal and Privacy Requirements
- The system shall protect students' personal information in accordance with applicable Vietnamese personal data protection laws and regulations.
- The system shall comply with Decree No. 13/2023/ND-CP on Personal Data Protection, where applicable.
- Student personal information shall only be collected and processed for legitimate course registration purposes.
- The system shall prevent unauthorized disclosure, modification, or deletion of student information.
- Access to personal data shall be restricted to authorized users only.
